arrays vs linked list 

both are a collection of data
    ....static arrays:  the lenght of the array is fixed at creation. it needs to be managed properly to prevent accessing out of bounds.
    
    ...dynamic saray: it is possible to change the length of the array, but the data stored in the old array would be copied 
        over into a new array, which increases the mem size.

    linked list: performs and structured differently to ana array
        ... contains nodes to store data, and each node points to another node, which creates a linked list
            the benefits of using a linked list is that a node can point anywhere, but it loses the ability to know exact location of a data point because you will not know the size immediately like an array.


