Static Arrays
A static array has a fixed size that must be known when the array is created.

Size is fixed and cannot change.
Memory is allocated once.
Elements are stored in contiguous memory.
Fast access using indexes (O(1)).
Simpler and has less memory overhead.

compiled vs interpreted languages.
compiled language converts the source code into 
machine code before execution which makes it faster 
because no translation happens while the code is running, 
but interpreted languages executes code at runtime through an interpreter, 
which makes execution slow. some compiled langauges are c/c++, rust or go, some interpreted languages are python, java script.